  "notes": "The first piece whose light does not travel in straight lines: every pixel integrates a null geodesic through a DNEG three-parameter wormhole. What the geometry bends is an accretion disk rather than only a sky, which is the difference between a smear and a readable scene \u2014 the far side of the disk arrives over the top of the throat and under the bottom of it at once. TWO boosts are applied and they multiply exactly: the camera's own motion, and the disk material's orbit, which is what makes one side white-hot and the other nearly gone. They multiply because g_tt is identically -1 here, so static observers all measure the same photon energy and there is no gravitational redshift anywhere in this spacetime \u2014 every colour change in the frame is kinematic. The sky's colour is a temperature rather than a hex code, which is what makes the shift exact; the disk's colour keeps that ordering and hands the hue to a ramp, because a Planck curve has no violet on it. uPalette 0 puts the physics back. uMode 1 draws the analytic crossing circle over the numerically classified pixels, uMode 3 shows where the radiance actually is, and uMode 4 the lensing magnification.",
